<title>FRANCE: EU sets nil value refund on wheat flour exports.</title>
<headline>EU sets nil value refund on wheat flour exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union will set a nil value refund on daily exports of soft wheat flour with effect from April 16, European Commission figures showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The refund on soft wheat flour currently stands at five Ecus per tonne.  </p>
<p>The move follows the abolition on Monday of the zero refund for wheat grain exports and its replacement with a nil value entry.</p>
<p>Unlike the zero refund the nil value refund cannot be prefixed and has no monthly increments.</p>
<p>On Tuesday exporters bid through France to export 217,000 tonnes of soft wheat under nil value licences and 214,500 tonnes of flour under licences carrying a five Ecus per tonne rebate, national grain office ONIC said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom 6331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
